IL metrics, ensuring proper handling of image files. Finally, the process posts handoff naming to `@anim`.\n\nAfter the server restart, verify upgraded animation scripts and incorporate fixes. If the environment build is not ready, the process will wait for the handoff from the environment agent. Once the stage environment blend is available, the build process can continue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"@monitor resume"}},{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"@env-2 Server restarted mid-turn — resume from where you left off (`pipeline/gen_textures.py` is already saved). Finish upgrading `pipeline/v5_env.py` incorporating all findings in #9 and #10 (`V5_Hangar` min track dist >= 180m, `V5_HedgeRing` radius >= 1500m, `V5_Stand_Complex` moved back `dist >= 38` so rail clears Copse track, `V5_Flag` `/255.0` linear albedo fix, dedicated single-user `Mat_FIA_RainLight`, smooth `V5_SkyDome` gradient, braking-zone skidmarks/DRS boards/pit timing, car paint/carbon/brake-rotor material polish, zero stranded root objects), run `v5_env.py` -> `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` and `v5_preview.py`, verify via Python PIL metrics (remember #7: NEVER call `read_file` on binary/image files), and post handoff naming `@anim`."}},{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"@anim Server restarted mid-turn — resume from where you left off (`v5_anim.py`, `v5_clay.py`, `v5_stills.py`, `v5_viewport_fast.py` edits are on disk). Remember #7 (NEVER call `read_file` on binary/image files; use Python PIL/numpy + Blender headless checks). Check #11 from `sfx` for the exact audio/mux commands & metrics to include in `README.md`, `LATEST/README.txt`, and `docs/README_V5.md`. Wait via `swarm_wait` if `@env-2` hasn't finished `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` yet; as soon as `@env-2` hands off, run final `v5_anim.py` -> `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend`, `v5_clay.py` -> `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `v5_viewport_fast.py` fast/normal check, render all 26 1080p color stills + contact sheet