\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:33:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":4095,\"cache_read_tokens\":157637,\"output_tokens\":2427,\"thinking\":\"`RIG_F1_Race` appears misplaced; it resides in the root scene collection instead of the intended `SCIFI_F1_2035` collection. This likely stems from a discrepancy in the referenced blend file. Moving the object within the scene collection hierarchy in the environment file should resolve the issue, maintaining its transformations.\\n\\n\\nThe `RIG_F1_Race` object's misplacement in the root scene collection is confirmed to stem from the blend file discrepancy, not the environment file itself. However, reviewing the `v5_anim.py` script reveals a critical oversight. The script's logic intended to group all car meshes except those prefixed with \\\"V5_\\\" or \\\"GEO_,\\\" but the condition was incorrectly written such that no car bodies were added, because the car meshes were prefixed with `GEO_`. This means the `V5_CarLightReceivers` collection does not have the cars.\\n\\n\\nThe bug in `v5_anim.py` on line 177, where the exclusion condition for car bodies was incorrectly written, has a significant impact; the car's body is not being illuminated by the fill lights. The car's body is not added to the `V5_CarLightReceivers` collection, meaning the three-point fill lights are only affecting decals, not the car's paint, clearcoat, or carbon fiber. Correcting the line will ensure proper lighting balance. Now, considering the broader upgrade strategy, a comprehensive review of the five mission areas is needed to refine the specifications for broadcast-grade textures and environment elements, aiming for under 1,050 objects and a 2.3s/frame CPU budget.\\n\\n\\nThe existing UV mapping of the pit garage indicates the need for a 2048x512 texture, representing six repeating garage bays across a 360m section. The UV coordinates map horizontally from 0.0 to 1.0 across the entire pit building and vertically from 0.0 to 2.0. This mapping requires verifying the current texture's representation in UV space using a script to avoid discrepancies.\\n\\n\\nThe pit garage UV mapping calculations must be rigorously checked in `v5_env.py`. Incorrect UV tiling would lead to unacceptable visual artifacts, especially with the intended resolution and scale. Current understanding of the texture layout hints at a 57 pixels per meter resolution, but needs confirmation.\\nA Python script to inspect existing texture structures, starting with `pit_garage.png`, `ad_boards.png`, and `bigscreen.png`, will verify assumptions and guide the texture generation process.\\n\\n\\nThe `bmesh.ops.create_cube` function, used within the `box()` function, requires immediate verification. It's crucial to confirm whether this function, when creating a cube, automatically generates UV coordinates. If not, the resulting cubes, such as the advertisement and screen boards, will lack UVs. Consequently, shader nodes like `ShaderNodeTexImage` will default to UV coordinates (0, 0), resulting in a single solid color on the boards due to the lack of proper UV mapping. A quick Blender check is underway to confirm if the `create_cube` function produces UVs by default.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"& \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\APPs\\\\\\\\steam\\\\\\\\steamapps\\\\\\\\common\\\\\\\\Blender\\\\\\\\blender.exe\\\\\\\" -b \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\项目session\\\\\\\\blender-supercar\\\\\\\\LATEST\\\\\\\\v5_stage_env.blend\\\\\\\" --python-expr \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport bpy\\\\nfor nm in ['V5_Ad_0', 'V5_Screen_A_Panel', 'V5_Brake_0_150', 'V5_PitGarageFront', 'V5_PitRoofBanner']:\\\\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.get(nm)\\\\n    if ob and ob.type == 'MESH':\\\\n        uvs = [l.name for l in ob.data.uv_layers]\\\\n        sample_uv = [tuple(round(x,3) for x in ob.data.uv_layers[0].data[i].uv) for i in range(min(8, len(ob.data.loops)))] if uvs else []\\\\n        print(f'{nm:22s}: uv_layers={uvs} sample={sample_uv}')\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check UV layers on textured V5 props\\\"\"}}]}\n48: {\"step_index\":47,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:34:16Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:34:16+08:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:34:20+08:00\\nCommand exited with code 0.\\n\\nCommand output:\\n                                                                                                   \\r\\n-- .-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------.   86052@Talonxus\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |   \\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |    Windows 11 家庭版 中文版 (26H2) x86_64\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |    Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 5 225H (4+10) @ 4.90 GHz\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |   󰚗 DRB-P-PCB (M1100)\\r\\n-- |  ,--.--------.     ,---.                      _,.---._      .-._                  ,-.--,  |    23.36 GiB / 31.50 GiB (74%)\\r\\n-- | /==/,  -   , -\\\\  .--.'  \\\\        _.-.       ,-.' , -  `.   /==/ \\\\  .-._  .--.-.  /=/, .'  |    278.09 GiB / 300.00 GiB (93%) - NTFS\\r\\n-- | \\\\==\\\\.-.  - ,-./  \\\\==\\\\-/\\\\ \\\\     .-,.'|      /==/_,  ,  - \\\\  |==|, \\\\/ /, / \\\\==\\\\ -\\\\/=/- /    |    548.10 GiB / 623.52 GiB (88%) - NTFS\\r\\n-- |  `--`\\\\==\\\\- \\\\     /==/-|_\\\\ |   |==|, |     |==|   .=.     | |==|-  \\\\|  |   \\\\==\\\\ `-' ,/     |    99.34 MiB / 3.13 GiB (3%) - NTFS\\r\\n-- |       \\\\==\\\\_ \\\\    \\\\==\\\\,   - \\\\  |==|- |     |==|_ : ;=:  - | |==| ,  | -|    |==|,  - |     |   \\r\\n-- |       |==|- |    /==/ -   ,|  |==|, |     |==| , '='     | |==| -   _ |   /==/   ,   \\\\    |   ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●\\r\\n-- |       |==|, |   /==/-  /\\\\ - \\\\ |==|- `-._   \\\\==\\\\ -    ,_ /  |==|  /\\\\ , |  /==/, .--, - \\\\   |\\r\\n-- |       /==/ -/   \\\\==\\\\ _.\\\\=\\\\.-' /==/ - , ,/   '.='. -   .'   /==/, | |- |  \\\\==\\\\- \\\\/=/ , /   |\\r\\n-- |       `--`--`    `--`         `--`-----'      `--`--''     `--`./  `--`   `--`-'  `--`    |\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |\\r\\n-- |                                                                                           |\\r\\n-- '-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------'\\r\\n00:00.672  blend            | Read blend: \\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\LATEST\\\\v5_stage_env.blend\\\"\\nBlenderMCP addon registered\\r\\nV5_Ad_0               : uv_layers=[] sample=[]\\r\\nV5_Screen_A_Panel     : uv_layers=[] sample=[]\\r\\nV5_Brake_0_150        : uv_layers=[] sample=[]\\r\\nV5_PitGarageFront     : uv_layers=['UVMap'] sample=[(0.0, 0.0), (0.0, 2.0), (0.006, 2.0), (0.006, 0.0), (0.006, 0.0), (0.006, 2.0), (0.011, 2.0), (0.011, 0.0)]\\r\\nV5_PitRoofBanner      : uv_layers=['UVMap'] sample=[(0.0, 0.0), (0.006, 0.0), (0.006, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (0.006, 0.0), (0.011, 0.0), (0.011, 1.0), (0.006, 1.0)]\\r\\nBlenderMCP addon unregistered\\r\\nBlender 5.3.0 (hash 02f0899d78e3 built 2026-11-10 01:33:43)\\n\\nBlender quit\\n\"}\n49: {\"step_index\":48,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:34:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":3560,\"cache_read_tokens\":161733,\"output_tokens\":846,\"thinking\":\"The output reveals specific image components, `V5_Ad_*`, `V5_Screen_*_Panel`, and `V5_Brake_*`, were processed but lack UV layers and samples, signifying incomplete rendering or data loading. This finding suggests a targeted area for inspection: the data handling process for these image components is not fully executing, or there is data corruption.\\n\\n\\nThe absence of UV layers and the rendering of single-pixel textures indicates a fundamental problem in the object creation process. The `bmesh.ops.create_cube` function was invoked without UV generation. This results in the complete failure of the texturing. A new panel object, with proper UV mapping, will resolve this. This panel object will be able to display the expected graphics.\\n\\n\\nThe updated panels correctly display the full screen graphic with the specified steel cabinet, indicating proper UV mapping and material application. Examining the pit garage texture, the original UV repeat values caused stretching. Adjusting the horizontal and vertical repeat values to match the bay spacing and garage design significantly improves the visual fidelity and architectural accuracy of the pit lane and associated banner.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"read_board\",\"args\":{\"since\":\"8\"}}]}\n50: {\"step_index\":49,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:34:42Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:34:42+08:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:34:43+08:00\\n{\\\"messages\\\":[],\\\"head\\\":8}\"}\n51: {\"step_index\":50,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:34:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":2063,\"cache_read_tokens\":164160,\"output_tokens\":10014,\"thinking\":\"Initial suspicion was that the orientation was handled directly with Euler angles. However, `v5_env.py` uses heading `h` as the track tangent angle, expressed as a forward vector. Therefore, need to verify how these track angles relate to the 3D model face orientations.\\n\\n\\nThe track tangent `h` directly defines the forward vector. Rotating the box object by `rot_z = h` aligns its local X-axis with the track's forward direction. However, brake boards and DRS boards require their widest face to be perpendicular to the track, directly facing the driver.\\n\\nThe current orientation, `rot_z = h`, is incorrect for these boards; the expected orientation requires a rotation of `rot_z = h + pi/2 - side * radians(12)` so the driver can see them head-on.\\n\\n\\nThe boards' facing is not solely determined by track tangent `h`. Brake and DRS boards require an orientation such that their broad faces are perpendicular to the track, directly towards the driver, achieved via the offset rotation `h + pi/2 - side * radians(12)`. Trackside sponsor hoardings and big screens require different orientations based on their placement and viewing angle relative to the track and oncoming traffic. The `panel_box` parameters are being reviewed.\\n\\n\\nThe UV mapping reveals specific material assignments: the broad faces use the main material, while the narrow edges use a steel material. Analysis confirms the intended orientations of different boards relative to the track tangent `h`. For brake and DRS boards, a 90-degree offset, `h + pi/2`, aligns their faces correctly towards the driver, with steel poles positioned on the sides.\\n\\n\\nThe environment objects' naming convention must start with \\\"V5_\\\" to ensure compatibility with existing scripts. The analysis of `v5_clay.py` and `v5_viewport_fast.py` confirms that objects need to be prefixed with \\\"V5_\\\" or \\\"LGT_V5\\\" and organized within specific scene collections. Unused assets will be removed to optimize file size and prevent errors.\\n\\n\\nChecking deceleration values from the track data reveals heavy braking zones \\n<truncated 7577 bytes>\\nearcoat and reduced emission for a flush appearance, referencing documentation advice to prevent plastic-like appearance at night. Adjusted carbon fiber materials for wings, floor, and other elements, to ensure that the roughness levels and clearcoat settings are optimized for a satin appearance.\\n\\n\\nObserved that current carbon fiber material setup only uses the weave texture for bump mapping, with fixed roughness values and unlinked texture coordinates. Corrected this by connecting texture coordinates to the noise texture's vector input. The weave pattern will now drive both the roughness and subtly vary the base color for carbon fiber materials, using a map range and color ramp. Added procedural weave roughness variation to wing endplates and brake ducts to catch light more realistically.\\n\\n\\nHalo's visual impact hinges on material choice, evaluating a titanium or carbon-titanium aesthetic for the halo hoop and pylon. Maintaining the refined `Mat_Liquid_Titanium` for the halo's central structure preserves its sleek look, while carbon fiber is applied to vortex fins.\\n\\nTire contrast examined, comparing the slick compound on tire tread vs. the sidewall material. Focusing on the tire's mesh, the center contact tread band needs adjustments, seeking a slightly heat-grained, satin-sheen appearance with subtle streaks and micro-graining for realistic rubber.\\n\\n\\nAdjusted the base color, roughness, and specular IOR for the tire tread material to simulate a heat-grained rubber effect, contrasting with the sidewall's matte finish. Fine-tuned the Pirelli sidewall material to provide a crisp satin-matte appearance against the tread. Brake rotor materials were identified and confirmed as `Mat_BrakeDisc_CarbonCeramic`.\\n\\n\\nThe brake thermal glow meshes were designed with an emission shader; however, setting the emission strength to zero and not using any transparency results in the brake glow objects being solid black when the brakes are cool. This is incorrect. The glow mesh needs to be invisible when the brakes are not glowing.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"read_board\",\"args\":{\"since\":\"8\"}},{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"& \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\APPs\\\\\\\\steam\\\\\\\\steamapps\\\\\\\\common\\\\\\\\Blender\\\\\\\\blender.exe\\\\\\\" -b \\\\\\\"D:\\\\\\\\项目session\\\\\\\\blender-supercar\\\\\\\\pipeline\\\\\\\\v4_stage_rig.blend\\\\\\\" --python-expr \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport bpy\\\\nfrom mathutils import Vector\\\\nfor nm in ['GEO_F1_Tire_FL', 'GEO_F1_Rim_FL', 'GEO_F1_RimSpokes_FL', 'GEO_F1_BrakeDisc_FL', 'GEO_F1_BrakeHoles_FL', 'GEO_F1_BrakeGlow_FL', 'GEO_F1_BrakeCaliper_FL', 'GEO_F1_BrakeDuct_FL']:\\\\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.get(nm)\\\\n    if ob:\\\\n        bb = [ob.matrix_world @ Vector(c) for c in ob.bound_box]\\\\n        mn = tuple(round(min(v[i] for v in bb), 4) for i in range(3))\\\\n        mx = tuple(round(max(v[i] for v in bb), 4) for i in range(3))\\\\n        lmn = tuple(round(min(v.co[i] for v in ob.data.vertices), 4) for i in range(3))\\\\n        lmx = tuple(round(max(v.co[i] for v in ob.data.vertices), 4) for i in range(3))\\\\n        vgs = [g.name for g in ob.vertex_groups]\\\\n        m = ob.data.materials[0] if ob.data.materials else None\\\\n        blend = getattr(m, 'surface_render_method', getattr(m, 'blend_method', None)) if m else None\\\\n        print(f'{nm:25s}: verts={len(ob.data.vertices):4d} hide_render={ob.hide_render} blend={blend} world_bb={mn}..{mx} local_bb={lmn}..{lmx} vgs={vgs}')\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect brake disc, glow, and tire geometry in v4_stage_rig.blend\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n52: {\"step_index\":51,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T05:37:18Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:37:18+08:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:37:26+08:00\\n{\\\"messages\\\":[{\\\"seq\\\":9,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"verifier\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"@env-2 @anim **ROUND 1 BASELINE AUDIT REPORT** (`v5_stage_env.blend`, `v5_stage_anim.blend`, `v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `frames/` \\\\u0026 `clay_frames/`)\\\\n\\\\n### P0 — Critical Bugs \\\\u0026 Obstructions Found\\\\n1. **`@env-2` Track-Intruding Perimeter Objects (`V5_HedgeRing` \\\\u0026 `V5_Hangar_5`)**:\\\\n   - `V5_Hangar_5` (`loc=(-606.8, 955.4)`, `dims=63.7x51.5m`, `min_dist_to_track=17.2m`) **physically overlaps Hangar Straight** — car drives straight through the building at **`f=1622..1632`** (`Cam_S19_Onboard3` occluded at 4.8–13.3m). `V5_Hangar_3` is also close (`94.4m`). **Fix**: reject/resample any hangar with `min_dist_to_track \\\\u003c 180m`.\\\\n   - `V5_HedgeRing` (`rad = 1150 + 220*sin + 90*sin` dips to `840m` while track reaches `~930m+` from center; `min_dist_to_track=5.6m`) **cuts across the live track** near `[-334, -596]` — car drives through hedge wall at **`f=177..179`** (`Cam_S02_Onboard`). **Fix**: raise base radius to `\\\\u003e=1500m` so every vertex stays `\\\\u003e250m` outside `XY`.\\\\n2. **`@anim` Broken Car Light-Linking Filter (`v5_anim.py:177`)**:\\\\n   - `not _ob.name.startswith((\\\\\\\"V5_\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"GEO_\\\\\\\"))` **excludes all 233 `GEO_F1_*` \\\\u0026 `GEO_MERC_*` car meshes** from `V5_CarLightReceivers`! Only the 10 `DEC_*` decal patches receive the `260+260+320W` `LGT_V5Car_0..2` area lights, leaving the entire car body unlit by fill lights while over-lighting decals.\\\\n   - **Fix**: include all 243 car meshes (`_ob.parent == rig` or `_ob.name.startswith((\\\\\\\"GEO_F1_\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"GEO_MERC_\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"DEC_\\\\\\\"))`), link/hide `V5_CarLightReceivers` cleanly (currently unlinked orphan collection), and balance `LGT_V5Car_*` energy so decals don't clip.\\\\n3. **`@env-2` 255x Over-Albedo Bug on Grandstand Flags (`v5_env.py:905`)**:\\\\n   - `V5_Flag_0..4` pass integer `0..255` tuples `(200,30,30)..(255,160,0)` into linear `Base Color` (`[240.0, 240.0, 240.0]`), causing extreme glare/clipping. Divide by `255.0` (and sc\\n<truncated 3905 bytes>\\nat `y=[0.12..0.19], z=[0.56..0.73]` and Halo pylon at `y=[0.40..0.58], z=[0.64..0.89]`, whereas BOTH `Cam_S02_Onboard` (`fwd=2.55`) \\\\u0026 `Cam_S19_Onboard3` (`fwd=2.48`) are on the nosecone tip! Placin